%% Proposed architecture, not an implemented or benchmarked system.
%% UK company, approximately 200 customers. Largest customer: up to 2 million movements.
%% Monthly interpretation is assumed. Total volume and input schemas remain unknown.
%% Invoice/receipt type, VAT rules, legal issue policy and billable components require validation.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Monthly scheduler
    participant C as Close and render workers - Python SQL LaTeX
    participant D as Operational DB - PostgreSQL
    actor U as Reviewer via Excel or web
    participant A as Control API - Python
    participant W as Dispatch worker - Python
    participant E as Email provider API
    participant V as Event receiver - Python

    S->>C: Close customer and accounting period
    C->>D: Acquire close-scope lock, verify source coverage, reconciliation and blockers
    Note over C,D: Processing all received rows does not establish source completeness.<br/>Use contracted manifests, counters or other source completion evidence.
    alt Required controls pass
        C->>D: Freeze consistent membership, source cutoffs, rules and captured scope generation
        C->>D: Reserve final document number and date under the agreed issuance policy
        Note over C,D: Reservation and rendering are not legal issuance.<br/>Any required date, number, content or recipient change creates a new package for review.<br/>Manage unused reservations according to the approved numbering policy.
        C->>C: Calculate exact decimal amounts, reconcile, build invoice JSON and exact email envelope
        C->>C: Escape data into versioned LaTeX, compile in isolation, upload and verify PDF
        C->>D: Publish immutable package, document fields, artifact hashes and READY_FOR_REVIEW
        U->>A: Open exact package preview
        A->>D: Read PDF, message, recipients, control evidence and package fingerprint
        A-->>U: Show final document and send envelope
        U->>A: Approve package ID, expected version and fingerprint
        A->>D: BEGIN, lock close scope and package, validate actor, generation, gates and fingerprint
        alt Current package and issuance policy permit approval-time issue
            A->>D: Claim stable billable components, record explicit ISSUE event, insert approval and outbox, COMMIT
            Note over A,D: Original issuance enforces UNIQUE issuer and stable billable-component identity.<br/>The constraint does not depend only on movement version: a correction cannot rebill the same component.<br/>Authorized adjustments use separate adjustment components linked to the original.<br/>Issue event, allocation claims, approval and dispatch job commit atomically in this policy path.
            A-->>U: ISSUED and APPROVED_QUEUED, with audit references
        else Explicit issue event already exists under the agreed policy
            A->>D: Verify issue event and exclusive component claims, insert approval and outbox, COMMIT
            Note over A,D: Record issuance at its agreed accounting event, not at PDF rendering or email delivery.<br/>This branch requires issue evidence that matches the exact approved document.<br/>Approval and outbox insertion are atomic, do not issue the same components again.
            A-->>U: Show actual issuance and approval states separately
        else Stale package, changed controls, duplicate component or issue-policy gate unmet
            A->>D: ROLLBACK, preserve conflict evidence
            A-->>U: Block dispatch, rebuild, reconcile or request authorized adjustment
        end
    else Required coverage or controls are missing
        C->>D: Record blocked close and evidence, produce no sendable package
    end

    opt Eligible approved dispatch exists
        opt Reviewer requests revocation before dispatch reservation
            U->>A: Revoke transport approval or request a replacement package
            A->>D: TX: lock same package and dispatch rows, revoke approval and cancel queued job
            Note over A,D: Cancelling transport does not undo an already recorded accounting ISSUE event.<br/>Issued document changes follow the authorized adjustment process.
        end

        W->>D: TX: same row locks, validate approval and fingerprint, reserve identified attempt, COMMIT
        alt Valid approval and eligible dispatch job
            D-->>W: Return immutable approved envelope and attempt reference
            Note over A,W: Revocation and reservation serialize through the same lock boundary.<br/>Once reservation succeeds, record cancellation requests but do not promise recall.<br/>Do not mutate the reserved payload or blindly reclaim an expired attempt lease.
            W->>E: Submit exact approved payload with stable attempt reference
            alt Provider definitely accepts
                E-->>W: Accepted and provider message ID
                W->>D: Record ACCEPTED and response evidence
            else Provider definitely rejects
                E-->>W: Definite rejection with error evidence
                W->>D: Record FAILED, classify retryability under provider contract
            else Timeout, lost response or worker crash creates ambiguity
                W->>D: Record or recover UNKNOWN, retain attempt and payload evidence
                Note over W,D: Lease expiry is not evidence that submission never happened.<br/>Do not automatically resubmit a potentially accepted attempt.
                W->>E: Reconcile by provider reference or supported request query
                alt Acceptance established
                    W->>D: Resolve ACCEPTED and bind provider message ID
                else Non-acceptance established or safe provider idempotency applies
                    W->>D: Authorize controlled retry using the same approved payload
                else Outcome remains uncertain or query is unsupported
                    W->>D: Keep UNKNOWN, require operational resolution
                end
            end
        else Revoked, cancelled, stale or otherwise ineligible
            D-->>W: Suppress submission and record reason
        end
    end

    opt Provider event is available at any time after submission
        E->>V: Delivery, bounce or delay event
        V->>D: Authenticate, deduplicate and append event, reconcile attempt correlation
        Note over V,D: Events may arrive before send-result persistence, out of order or repeatedly.<br/>Retain unmatched events for reconciliation and keep occurrence plus receipt times.<br/>A delivery event can be followed by a bounce.
    end
    Note over U,V: Keep dispatch, delivery and customer acknowledgement as separate evidence dimensions.<br/>Provider acceptance is not delivery, server delivery is not human reading.<br/>Only an explicit authenticated customer action records acknowledgement.
